'Britain's relations with dominions grew more distant during the period 1918 to 1939.' Assess the validity of this view.

Evidence to support:-

Growing Autonomy:
- Balfour Definition, 1926
- Statue of Westminster, 1931 -> Legal autonomy, independence

Growing Nationalism:
- Growing assertiveness of Colonial identities (links to WW1)
- Afrikaner Nationalism (Herzog, Anti-British)
- Anglo-Irish Treaty, 1921 (treaty-ports during WW2)
- Bodyline Affair, 1932

Evidence to challenge:-

Growing Economic links:
- Great Depression
- Ottawa Conference, 1932
- Sterling Area
- Growth in inter-dominion trade

Migration - cultural links, language

Strategic military planning - preparations for WWII - role of dominions in WWII
